    {
      "v": 3,
      "zh": "我见你们不来救我，我就拚命前去攻击亚扪人，耶和华将他们交在我手中。你们今日为甚么上我这里来攻打我呢？」",
      "en": "When I saw that you were not going to help,[NOTE:1] I risked my life[NOTE:2] and advanced against[NOTE:3] the Ammonites, and the Lord handed them over to me. Why have you come up[NOTE:4] to fight with me today?”",
      "notes": [
        "Heb “you were no deliverer.” Codex Alexandrinus (A) of the LXX has “no one was helping.”",
        "Heb “I put my life in my hand.”",
        "Heb “crossed over to.”",
        "The Hebrew adds “against me” here. This is redundant in English and has not been included in the translation for stylistic reasons."
