      "v": 5,
      "zh": "基列人把守约旦河的渡口，不容以法莲人过去。以法莲逃走的人若说：「容我过去。」基列人就问他说：「你是以法莲人不是？」他若说：「不是」，",
      "en": "The Gileadites captured the fords of the Jordan River[NOTE:1] opposite Ephraim.[NOTE:2] Whenever an Ephraimite fugitive[NOTE:3] said, “Let me cross over,” the men of Gilead asked[NOTE:4] him, “Are you an Ephraimite?” If he said, “No,”",
      "notes": [
        "The word “River” is not in the Hebrew text, but is supplied in the translation for clarification.",
        "Or “against Ephraim,” that is, so as to prevent Ephraim from crossing.",
        "The Hebrew text has a plural form here.",
        "Heb “say to.”"
